"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Use batch mode to submit multiple primitive jobs simultaneously. Following are examples of working with batches.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set up to use batches {#set-up-to-use-batches}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before starting a batch, you must [set up the IBM Quantum Compute "
"client](/guides/install-qiskit) and initialize it as a service:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Open a batch {#open-a-batch}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can open a runtime batch by using the context manager `with Batch(...)` or by initializing the `Batch`\n"
"class. When you start a batch,  you must specify a QPU by passing a `backend` object.  The batch starts when its first job begins execution.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Batch class**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Context manager**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The context manager automatically opens and closes the batch.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"specify-batch-length\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Batch length {#batch-length}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can define the batch's maximum time to live (TTL) with the `max_time` "
"parameter. This should exceed the longest job's execution time. This timer "
"starts when the batch starts.  When the value is reached, the batch is "
"closed.  Any jobs that are running will finish, but jobs still queued are "
"failed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There is also an interactive time to live (interactive TTL) value that "
"cannot be configured (1 minute for all plans).  If no batch jobs are queued "
"within that window, the batch is temporarily deactivated.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Default maximum TTL values:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Instance type  | Default Maximum TTL |\n"
"|----------------|---------------------|\n"
"| All paid plans | 8 hours             |\n"
"| Open           | 10 minutes          |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To determine a batch's maximum TTL or interactive TTL, follow the "
"instructions in [Determine batch details](#batch-details) and look for the "
"`max_time` or `interactive_timeout` value, respectively.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"close\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Close a batch {#close-a-batch}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A batch automatically closes when it exits the context manager. When the "
"batch context manager is exited, the batch is put into \"In progress, not "
"accepting new jobs\" status. This means that the batch finishes processing "
"all running or queued jobs until the maximum TTL value is reached. After all"
" jobs are completed, the batch is immediately closed. You cannot submit jobs"
" to a closed batch.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The following code requires that you supply your own information, such as Estimator and Sampler PUBs, and a backend.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"If you are not using a context manager, manually close the batch.  If you leave the batch open and submit more jobs to it later, it is possible that the maximum TTL will be reached before the subsequent jobs start running; causing them to be canceled. You can close a batch as soon as you are done submitting jobs to it. When a batch is closed with `batch.close()`, it no longer accepts new jobs, but the already submitted jobs will still run until completion and their results can be retrieved.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"batch-details\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Determine batch details {#determine-batch-details}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a comprehensive overview of a batch's configuration and status, "
"including its interactive and max TTL, use the  `batch.details() method`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"partition\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reconfigure jobs for parallel processing {#reconfigure-jobs-for-parallel-"
"processing}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are multiple ways you can reconfigure your jobs to take advantage of "
"the parallel processing provided by batching. The following example shows "
"how you can partition a long list of circuits into multiple jobs and run "
"them as a batch to take advantage of the parallel processing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"If you set `backend=backend` in a primitive, the program is run in job mode, even if it's inside a batch or session context. Setting `backend=backend` is deprecated as of Qiskit Runtime v0.24.0.  Instead, use the `mode` parameter.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

